cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use kanji1024, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "kanji1024: a binary-to-text encoding over the 1026 kyōiku kanji"
abstract: >-
  kanji1024 writes arbitrary bytes as the kanji taught in Japanese primary
  school, ten bits per character, with an optional 20-bit checksum. This
  release contains the specification, the character table, a reference
  library, a command line tool and a browser workbench.
authors:
  - name: "Aesthetic Vulpes"
    website: "https://github.com/didvc/"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-31
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/didvc/kanji1024"
url: "https://didvc.github.io/kanji1024/"
keywords:
  - binary-to-text encoding
  - kanji
  - kyōiku kanji
  - checksum
  - human-readable identifiers
